  <!--
    Optim's user-facing strings. This is the neutral (en-US) resource.

    To add a language, copy this file to Strings/<bcp-47-tag>/Resources.resw
    (for example Strings/de-DE/Resources.resw) and translate only the <value>
    elements. Keys must stay identical; any key a translated file omits falls
    back to the value here, so a partial translation is safe to ship.

    XAML resolves these through x:Uid: an element with x:Uid="Nav_Home" reads
    Nav_Home.Content, x:Uid on a SettingsCard reads .Header / .Description.
    Code resolves them through Optim.App.Localization.Loc.Get, which always
    takes an English fallback so a missing key can never blank the UI.
  -->

